# Copy to .env.local for local development, or set these in
# Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables for a deployment.
# Every one of them is optional: with none set the app still runs, it just
# keeps ratings in function memory and serves catalog text for descriptions.
# See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md for what each one turns on.

# --- Rating storage (Upstash Redis / Vercel KV) -----------------------------
# Without these, votes are stored per-instance in memory and are lost on a cold
# start. Vercel injects them automatically when you attach a KV store to the
# project. GET /api/status reports whether they took effect.
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
# Connecting to Upstash directly instead of through Vercel? These are read too.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# --- Course description provider -------------------------------------------
# The third-party summariser behind GET /api/description/:courseId.
# Contract and response shape: docs/input.md
DESCRIPTION_API_URL=
DESCRIPTION_API_KEY=
# Send the key in a header other than Authorization (raw, no "Bearer " prefix).
# DESCRIPTION_API_AUTH_HEADER=X-Api-Key
# DESCRIPTION_API_TIMEOUT_MS=8000
# DESCRIPTION_CACHE_TTL_S=604800

# --- Cross-origin access ----------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated origins allowed to make *credentialed* calls (ones carrying
# the voter cookie). The project's own Vercel URL is always trusted. Everyone
# else still gets the open anonymous API, just without the cookie.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-domain.example,https://www.your-domain.example

# --- Limits -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Requests per 10-minute window, per voter (falling back to IP).
# RATE_LIMIT_VOTES=60
# RATE_LIMIT_DESCRIPTIONS=60
# Largest accepted request body, in bytes.
# MAX_BODY_BYTES=16384
